cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software in research, please cite it.
title: "edf2csv: a command-line converter from EDF, EDF+ and BDF recordings to CSV"
abstract: >-
  edf2csv converts EDF, EDF+ and BDF biosignal recordings to CSV from the command
  line. It runs locally, streams so that memory does not grow with recording length,
  and is deliberately conservative with the data: channels recorded at different
  sampling rates are written to separate files rather than resampled onto a common
  grid, units are never converted, discontinuous recordings keep their real timing,
  and malformed files are reported rather than silently producing plausible output.
  Physical values are verified against pyEDFlib.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tayal
    given-names: Sarthak
repository-code: https://github.com/tayal-sarthak/edf2csv
url: https://edf2csv.vercel.app
license: MIT
